codemap 8
path lsp-client
kind layer
author ai
group index
note A minimal language-server client, the io-lsp crate: JSON-RPC over the spawned server's stdio, and nothing more of the protocol than this tool needs. session.rs is LspSession, the client; wire.rs builds and reads the JSON (Outgoing requests, the framing, the shapes of answers); convert.rs turns answers into domain and answer.rs types, with URIs mapped to root-relative paths. Requests are synchronous - a reader thread queues every incoming message and request blocks for the matching id, servicing notifications and the server's own requests as they go by, which is what keeps a chatty server from deadlocking. The index crate's server.rs uses it for document symbols, outgoing calls, incoming calls and references, and the GUI's server thread for hover, definition and references. Everything about it is shaped by one fact: a server takes seconds to become useful, so wait_ready exists and the answers are cached. Positions are 0-based like LSP's own and columns are UTF-16 units. Only start returns an error; a query whose answer never came or was an error reads as empty or None. The test that drives a real server needs rust-analyzer on PATH and runs only with cargo test -- --ignored.

